program: char_cast_negative_trap.lu
trap:    overflow
clause:  [type.char.cast]
rule:    CharCast
message: `-1 as char`: the value is negative, and no scalar is — it names no character, and admitting it would mint a `char` that cannot be UTF-8-encoded (D24), so the cast traps ([type.char.cast], D56's family)
at:      13:13 `n as char`
because: (single-span fault)
